msgid "Design principles of operator representations {#design-principles-of-operator-representations}"
msgstr "Prinsip reka bentuk perwakilan pengendali {#design-principles-of-operator-representations}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This guide explains how a [`BosonOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator\") is organized and how to work with it: how to build one, how to inspect and combine operators, and how to bring two operators into a form where they can be compared. Start here when you write down a Hamiltonian.\n"
msgstr "Panduan ini menerangkan cara [`BosonOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator\") disusun dan cara bekerja dengannya: cara membina satu, cara memeriksa dan menggabungkan pengendali, dan cara membawa dua pengendali ke dalam bentuk yang boleh dibandingkan. Mulakan di sini apabila anda menulis Hamiltonian.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A [`BosonOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator\") is an exact sum of products of bosonic creation and annihilation operators with complex coefficients. It carries no occupation cutoff. A bosonic mode holds arbitrarily many bosons, so its Fock space is infinite-dimensional, and a truncation enters only when the operator is mapped onto qubits (see [Truncate the Fock space](mappers#truncation-explanation)). Everything in this guide therefore happens in the exact algebra of the canonical commutation relations,\n"
msgstr "[`BosonOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator\") ialah hasil tambah tepat bagi hasil darab pengendali penciptaan dan pemusnahan bosonik dengan pekali kompleks. Ia tidak mempunyai had penghunian. Satu mod bosonik boleh memuatkan boson dalam bilangan sembarangan, jadi ruang Fock-nya berdimensi tak terhingga, dan pemangkasan hanya berlaku apabila pengendali dipetakan ke qubit (lihat [Memangkas ruang Fock](mappers#truncation-explanation)). Oleh itu, segala-galanya dalam panduan ini berlaku dalam aljabar tepat hubungan kekomutan kanonik,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"[b_i, b_j^\\dagger] = \\delta_{ij}, \\qquad [b_i, b_j] = [b_i^\\dagger, b_j^\\dagger] = 0 \\, .\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"[b_i, b_j^\\dagger] = \\delta_{ij}, \\qquad [b_i, b_j] = [b_i^\\dagger, b_j^\\dagger] = 0 \\, .\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Two consequences shape the interface. A mode index can repeat within a single term, because $b_i^\\dagger b_i^\\dagger$ is a valid operator that creates two bosons. Also, reordering two factors never introduces a sign, although moving an annihilation operator past a creation operator on the same mode adds a term, $b_i b_i^\\dagger = b_i^\\dagger b_i + 1$.\n"
msgstr "Dua akibat membentuk antara muka ini. Indeks mod boleh berulang dalam satu sebutan, kerana $b_i^\\dagger b_i^\\dagger$ ialah pengendali sah yang mencipta dua boson. Selain itu, menyusun semula dua faktor tidak pernah memperkenalkan tanda, walaupun menggerakkan pengendali pemusnahan melepasi pengendali penciptaan pada mod yang sama menambah satu sebutan, $b_i b_i^\\dagger = b_i^\\dagger b_i + 1$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Storage {#storage}"
msgstr "Storan {#storage}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "An operator keeps its terms in four flat arrays, similar to the compressed sparse row format of a sparse matrix:\n"
msgstr "Pengendali menyimpan sebutannya dalam empat tatasusunan rata, serupa dengan format baris jarang termampat bagi matriks jarang:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"|              |                                                                                         |\n"
"| ------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| `coeffs`     | One complex coefficient per term.                                                       |\n"
"| `actions`    | One boolean per factor: `True` for a creation and `False` for an annihilation operator. |\n"
"| `modes`      | One mode index per factor.                                                              |\n"
"| `boundaries` | The positions in `actions` and `modes` where each term starts and ends.                 |\n"
msgstr ""
"|              |                                                                                         |\n"
"| ------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| `coeffs`     | Satu pekali kompleks bagi setiap sebutan.                                               |\n"
"| `actions`    | Satu boolean bagi setiap faktor: `True` untuk penciptaan dan `False` untuk pengendali pemusnahan. |\n"
"| `modes`      | Satu indeks mod bagi setiap faktor.                                                     |\n"
"| `boundaries` | Kedudukan dalam `actions` dan `modes` di mana setiap sebutan bermula dan berakhir.      |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The constructor takes these four arrays directly. The operator below has three terms, namely $2 b_0^\\dagger b_1$, $-i b_1^\\dagger b_1^\\dagger$, and the constant $0.5$, and you can read the arrays back with the `get_*` methods:\n"
msgstr "Pembina menerima keempat-empat tatasusunan ini secara terus. Pengendali di bawah mempunyai tiga sebutan, iaitu $2 b_0^\\dagger b_1$, $-i b_1^\\dagger b_1^\\dagger$, dan pemalar $0.5$, dan anda boleh membaca semula tatasusunan tersebut dengan kaedah `get_*`:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The first term spans positions 0 to 2 of `actions` and `modes`, the second spans 2 to 4, and the third spans 4 to 4, which is how the constant term, a term without factors, is stored. The repeated mode `1` in the second term is preserved as written; a term is never dropped or merged because a mode index appears twice.\n"
msgstr "Sebutan pertama merentangi kedudukan 0 hingga 2 bagi `actions` dan `modes`, yang kedua merentangi 2 hingga 4, dan yang ketiga merentangi 4 hingga 4, iaitu cara sebutan pemalar, sebutan tanpa faktor, disimpan. Mod `1` yang berulang dalam sebutan kedua dikekalkan seperti yang ditulis; sesuatu sebutan tidak pernah dibuang atau digabungkan kerana indeks mod muncul dua kali.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  An operator built with [`from_dict()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.from_dict \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.from_dict\") does not store its terms in the order of the dictionary, so its arrays can list the terms in a different order from run to run. The operator itself is the same, and nothing below that compares or prints operators depends on the stored order.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Pengendali yang dibina dengan [`from_dict()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.from_dict \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.from_dict\") tidak menyimpan sebutannya mengikut tertib kamus, jadi tatasusunannya boleh menyenaraikan sebutan dalam tertib berbeza dari satu larian ke larian yang lain. Pengendali itu sendiri sama, dan tiada apa di bawah yang membandingkan atau mencetak pengendali bergantung pada tertib simpanan.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The layout makes construction and arithmetic cheap, with one consequence: an operator can hold the same term several times at once. Sums and products append terms and do not merge them, so call [`simplify()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.simplify \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.simplify\") when you need unique terms (see [Do arithmetic](#operators-arithmetic)).\n"
msgstr "Susun atur ini menjadikan pembinaan dan aritmetik murah, dengan satu akibat: pengendali boleh memegang sebutan yang sama beberapa kali serentak. Hasil tambah dan hasil darab menambah sebutan dan tidak menggabungkannya, jadi panggil [`simplify()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.simplify \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.simplify\") apabila anda memerlukan sebutan unik (lihat [Melakukan aritmetik](#operators-arithmetic)).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Build operators {#build-operators}"
msgstr "Membina pengendali {#build-operators}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The most direct way to build an operator is [`from_dict()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.from_dict \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.from_dict\"), which takes a dictionary from a tuple of factors to a coefficient. The functions [`cre()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-cre#qiskit_bosons.operators.cre \"qiskit_bosons.operators.cre\") and [`ann()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-ann#qiskit_bosons.operators.ann \"qiskit_bosons.operators.ann\") create the factors, and the empty tuple is the constant term:\n"
msgstr "Cara paling terus untuk membina pengendali ialah [`from_dict()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.from_dict \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.from_dict\"), yang menerima kamus daripada tuple faktor kepada pekali. Fungsi [`cre()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-cre#qiskit_bosons.operators.cre \"qiskit_bosons.operators.cre\") dan [`ann()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-ann#qiskit_bosons.operators.ann \"qiskit_bosons.operators.ann\") mencipta faktor, dan tuple kosong ialah sebutan pemalar:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the printed form, `+0` stands for $b_0^\\dagger$ and `-0` for $b_0$. The constructors [`zero()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.zero \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.zero\") and [`one()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.one \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.one\") return the additive and the multiplicative identity, and [`from_terms()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.from_terms \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.from_terms\") rebuilds an operator from the iterator of [`iter_terms()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.iter_terms \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.iter_terms\").\n"
msgstr "Dalam bentuk bercetak, `+0` mewakili $b_0^\\dagger$ dan `-0` mewakili $b_0$. Pembina [`zero()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.zero \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.zero\") dan [`one()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.one \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.one\") mengembalikan identiti penambahan dan pendaraban, dan [`from_terms()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.from_terms \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.from_terms\") membina semula pengendali daripada iterator [`iter_terms()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.iter_terms \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.iter_terms\").\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The operator library provides the dimensionless position and momentum quadratures,\n"
msgstr "Pustaka pengendali menyediakan kuadratur kedudukan dan momentum tanpa dimensi,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{q} = \\frac{b^\\dagger + b}{\\sqrt{2}}, \\qquad\n"
"\\hat{p} = \\frac{i \\left(b^\\dagger - b\\right)}{\\sqrt{2}} \\, ,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{q} = \\frac{b^\\dagger + b}{\\sqrt{2}}, \\qquad\n"
"\\hat{p} = \\frac{i \\left(b^\\dagger - b\\right)}{\\sqrt{2}} \\, ,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "as [`position()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-library-position#qiskit_bosons.operators.library.position \"qiskit_bosons.operators.library.position\") and [`momentum()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-library-momentum#qiskit_bosons.operators.library.momentum \"qiskit_bosons.operators.library.momentum\"). Together with the commutator functions of the same module, you can check the algebra directly:\n"
msgstr "sebagai [`position()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-library-position#qiskit_bosons.operators.library.position \"qiskit_bosons.operators.library.position\") dan [`momentum()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-library-momentum#qiskit_bosons.operators.library.momentum \"qiskit_bosons.operators.library.momentum\"). Bersama fungsi komutator dalam modul yang sama, anda boleh menyemak aljabar secara terus:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The module also provides [`anti_commutator()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-library-anti-commutator#qiskit_bosons.operators.library.anti_commutator \"qiskit_bosons.operators.library.anti_commutator\") and [`double_commutator()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-library-double-commutator#qiskit_bosons.operators.library.double_commutator \"qiskit_bosons.operators.library.double_commutator\"). All three take operators of the same type and return a new operator.\n"
msgstr "Modul ini juga menyediakan [`anti_commutator()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-library-anti-commutator#qiskit_bosons.operators.library.anti_commutator \"qiskit_bosons.operators.library.anti_commutator\") dan [`double_commutator()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-library-double-commutator#qiskit_bosons.operators.library.double_commutator \"qiskit_bosons.operators.library.double_commutator\"). Ketiga-tiganya menerima pengendali berjenis sama dan mengembalikan pengendali baharu.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"operators-product-order\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Mind the order of a product {#mind-the-order-of-a-product}"
msgstr "Perhatikan tertib hasil darab {#mind-the-order-of-a-product}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Two operators can be multiplied in two ways, and they are easy to confuse. The `@` operator is the mathematical product, so `a @ b` is $AB$. The `&` operator is *composition*, which follows Qiskit’s convention of reading from left to right: `a & b` first applies `a` and then `b`, so it is $BA$. The commutator functions use `@`, so `commutator(a, b)` is $[A, B]$. Building the bracket yourself out of `&` silently negates it:\n"
msgstr "Dua pengendali boleh didarab dalam dua cara, dan keduanya mudah dikelirukan. Pengendali `@` ialah hasil darab matematik, jadi `a @ b` ialah $AB$. Pengendali `&` ialah *gubahan*, yang mengikut konvensyen Qiskit iaitu membaca dari kiri ke kanan: `a & b` mengaplikasikan `a` dahulu kemudian `b`, jadi ia ialah $BA$. Fungsi komutator menggunakan `@`, jadi `commutator(a, b)` ialah $[A, B]$. Membina kurungan itu sendiri menggunakan `&` menafikannya secara senyap:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Inspect an operator {#inspect-an-operator}"
msgstr "Memeriksa pengendali {#inspect-an-operator}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "An operator is not directly iterable, because its terms live in the flat arrays above. Use [`iter_terms()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.iter_terms \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.iter_terms\") instead, which yields a list of `(is_creation, mode)` pairs and a coefficient for each term. The iterator returns copies, so changing them does not change the operator.\n"
msgstr "Pengendali tidak boleh diiterasi secara langsung, kerana sebutannya berada dalam tatasusunan rata di atas. Gunakan [`iter_terms()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.iter_terms \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.iter_terms\") sebaliknya, yang menghasilkan senarai pasangan `(is_creation, mode)` dan satu pekali bagi setiap sebutan. Iterator mengembalikan salinan, jadi mengubahnya tidak mengubah pengendali.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Several methods summarize the structure of an operator:\n"
msgstr "Beberapa kaedah meringkaskan struktur pengendali:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[`get_support()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.get_support \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.get_support\") is the set of modes the operator acts on, [`min_num_modes()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.min_num_modes \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.min_num_modes\") is the smallest register that can hold it, and [`max_rank()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.max_rank \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.max_rank\") is the length of its longest term.\n"
msgstr "[`get_support()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.get_support \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.get_support\") ialah set mod yang menjadi sasaran pengendali, [`min_num_modes()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.min_num_modes \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.min_num_modes\") ialah register terkecil yang boleh memuatkannya, dan [`max_rank()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.max_rank \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.max_rank\") ialah panjang sebutan terpanjangnya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  A **mode** is an abstract index that labels one bosonic degree of freedom. It has no meaning of its own: you determine which site of a lattice, which vibrational coordinate or which optical port a mode stands for. The [`BosonicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-bosonic-circuit#qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit\") uses the same indices (see [Work with bosonic circuits](circuit#bosonic-circuit-explanation)), so an operator and the gates that carry it agree on what mode `2` is without either one knowing what it represents. Nothing in the operator fixes how many levels a mode has, which is also why the register size is only a lower bound; [`min_num_modes()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.min_num_modes \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.min_num_modes\") is the smallest register that holds the operator, not a property of it.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  **Mod** ialah indeks abstrak yang melabelkan satu darjah kebebasan bosonik. Ia tidak mempunyai makna sendiri: anda yang menentukan tapak kekisi, koordinat getaran, atau port optik yang diwakili oleh sesuatu mod. [`BosonicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-bosonic-circuit#qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit\") menggunakan indeks yang sama (lihat [Bekerja dengan litar bosonik](circuit#bosonic-circuit-explanation)), jadi pengendali dan gate yang membawanya bersetuju tentang apa itu mod `2` tanpa salah satunya mengetahui apa yang diwakilinya. Tiada apa dalam pengendali yang menetapkan bilangan aras bagi sesuatu mod, dan itu juga sebab saiz register hanyalah had bawah; [`min_num_modes()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.min_num_modes \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.min_num_modes\") ialah register terkecil yang memuatkan pengendali, bukan sifatnya.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The occupation methods report how many bosons a single term can place in one mode. This is a lower bound on the cutoff that a mapping needs. It is not a sufficient cutoff, because repeated applications of the operator, as in a time evolution, can populate higher levels (see [Truncate the Fock space](mappers#truncation-explanation)):\n"
msgstr "Kaedah penghunian melaporkan bilangan boson yang boleh diletakkan oleh satu sebutan dalam satu mod. Ini ialah had bawah bagi had yang diperlukan oleh pemetaan. Ia bukan had yang mencukupi, kerana aplikasi pengendali berulang, seperti dalam evolusi masa, boleh menghuni aras yang lebih tinggi (lihat [Memangkas ruang Fock](mappers#truncation-explanation)):\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Two further checks look at conserved quantities. An operator conserves the particle number when every term has as many creation as annihilation operators. Passing a list of block sizes tests the same condition within each block of consecutive modes:\n"
msgstr "Dua semakan lanjut melihat kuantiti terabadi. Pengendali mengekalkan bilangan zarah apabila setiap sebutan mempunyai pengendali penciptaan dan pemusnahan yang sama banyak. Menghantar senarai saiz blok menguji syarat yang sama dalam setiap blok mod berturutan:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Finally, [`relabel_modes()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.relabel_modes \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.relabel_modes\") renames modes: mode `i` becomes `permutation[i]`. The list must be long enough to index every mode of the operator and must not repeat an entry:\n"
msgstr "Akhir sekali, [`relabel_modes()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.relabel_modes \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.relabel_modes\") menamakan semula mod: mod `i` menjadi `permutation[i]`. Senarai mestilah cukup panjang untuk mengindeks setiap mod pengendali dan tidak boleh mengulang entri:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"operators-arithmetic\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Do arithmetic {#do-arithmetic}"
msgstr "Melakukan aritmetik {#do-arithmetic}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Operators support addition, subtraction, negation, and multiplication and division by a number, in the usual operator form or in place:\n"
msgstr "Pengendali menyokong penambahan, penolakan, penafian, serta pendaraban dan pembahagian dengan nombor, dalam bentuk pengendali biasa atau di tempat:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The three terms of `total` were never merged, so the operator held `b_dag` twice until [`simplify()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.simplify \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.simplify\") combined them. The method sums the coefficients of identical terms and drops those whose total magnitude is below a tolerance. It is a structural operation: it compares the written factors and does *not* apply the commutation relations. The related method [`ichop()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.ichop \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.ichop\") removes small coefficients in place without merging first, so call [`simplify()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.simplify \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.simplify\") before [`ichop()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.ichop \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.ichop\") when an operator can hold duplicate terms.\n"
msgstr "Tiga sebutan `total` tidak pernah digabungkan, jadi pengendali memegang `b_dag` dua kali sehingga [`simplify()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.simplify \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.simplify\") menggabungkannya. Kaedah ini menjumlahkan pekali sebutan yang sama dan membuang sebutan yang magnitud jumlahnya di bawah toleransi. Ia ialah operasi struktur: ia membandingkan faktor yang ditulis dan *tidak* mengaplikasikan hubungan kekomutan. Kaedah berkaitan [`ichop()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.ichop \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.ichop\") membuang pekali kecil di tempat tanpa menggabungkan dahulu, jadi panggil [`simplify()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.simplify \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.simplify\") sebelum [`ichop()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.ichop \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.ichop\") apabila pengendali boleh memegang sebutan pendua.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Products use `@` or `&` as described above, and `**` raises an operator to an integer power:\n"
msgstr "Hasil darab menggunakan `@` atau `&` seperti yang diterangkan di atas, dan `**` menaikkan pengendali kepada kuasa integer:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The result lists the four orderings as written. Reducing them to a single form needs the commutation relations, which the next section applies.\n"
msgstr "Keputusan menyenaraikan empat susunan seperti yang ditulis. Memudahkannya kepada satu bentuk memerlukan hubungan kekomutan, yang diaplikasikan oleh bahagian seterusnya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The adjoint reverses the order of the factors in each term, exchanges creation and annihilation operators, and conjugates the coefficients. The method [`is_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.is_hermitian \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.is_hermitian\") tests whether an operator equals its adjoint:\n"
msgstr "Adjoin membalikkan tertib faktor dalam setiap sebutan, menukar pengendali penciptaan dan pemusnahan, serta mengkonjugat pekali. Kaedah [`is_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.is_hermitian \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.is_hermitian\") menguji sama ada pengendali sama dengan adjoinnya:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A lone hopping term is not Hermitian, which matters when you group terms for a time evolution: each group must be Hermitian on its own (see [Group operator terms: use the operator structure](grouping#grouping-explanation)).\n"
msgstr "Sebutan lompatan tunggal bukan Hermitian, yang penting apabila anda mengumpulkan sebutan untuk evolusi masa: setiap kumpulan mestilah Hermitian dengan sendirinya (lihat [Mengumpulkan sebutan pengendali: gunakan struktur pengendali](grouping#grouping-explanation)).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Normal order and compare operators {#normal-order-and-compare-operators}"
msgstr "Tertib normal dan membandingkan pengendali {#normal-order-and-compare-operators}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Two products of ladder operators can be the same operator and still look different, because $b\\,b^\\dagger$ and $b^\\dagger b + 1$ are equal in the algebra. Operators that are equal in this sense need not be stored equally, so comparing them needs the commutation relations. The method [`normal_ordered()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.normal_ordered \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.normal_ordered\") applies them: it moves every creation operator to the left of every annihilation operator and adds a term whenever a pair on the same mode is exchanged.\n"
msgstr "Dua hasil darab pengendali tangga boleh menjadi pengendali yang sama namun kelihatan berbeza, kerana $b\\,b^\\dagger$ dan $b^\\dagger b + 1$ adalah sama dalam aljabar. Pengendali yang sama dalam erti kata ini tidak semestinya disimpan sama, jadi membandingkannya memerlukan hubungan kekomutan. Kaedah [`normal_ordered()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.normal_ordered \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.normal_ordered\") mengaplikasikannya: ia memindahkan setiap pengendali penciptaan ke sebelah kiri setiap pengendali pemusnahan dan menambah sebutan setiap kali pasangan pada mod yang sama ditukar.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The ordered operator is returned as an unmerged sum, with five stored terms that reduce to three after [`simplify()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.simplify \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.simplify\") merges them. Normal ordering never makes a term vanish: $b^\\dagger b^\\dagger$ and every other repeated factor stay.\n"
msgstr "Pengendali bertertib dikembalikan sebagai hasil tambah tidak bergabung, dengan lima sebutan tersimpan yang menjadi tiga selepas [`simplify()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.simplify \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.simplify\") menggabungkannya. Tertib normal tidak pernah menyebabkan sebutan lenyap: $b^\\dagger b^\\dagger$ dan setiap faktor berulang yang lain kekal.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `sandwich` argument sets how the modes inside the two groups of factors are arranged. By default both groups are sorted in descending order. With `sandwich=True`, the creation operators are ascending and the annihilation operators descending, which puts the larger indices towards the middle:\n"
msgstr "Argumen `sandwich` menetapkan cara mod di dalam dua kumpulan faktor disusun. Secara lalai kedua-dua kumpulan diisih secara menurun. Dengan `sandwich=True`, pengendali penciptaan menaik dan pengendali pemusnahan menurun, yang meletakkan indeks lebih besar ke arah tengah:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `==` operator tests exact equality of the stored terms, with no tolerance and no simplification, so it can report a difference between two operators that are mathematically equal. The method [`equiv()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.equiv \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.equiv\") brings the difference of the two operators to normal order first and then tests that every coefficient is below a tolerance. It is the comparison you almost always want:\n"
msgstr "Pengendali `==` menguji kesamaan tepat bagi sebutan tersimpan, tanpa toleransi dan tanpa pemudahan, jadi ia boleh melaporkan perbezaan antara dua pengendali yang sama secara matematik. Kaedah [`equiv()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.equiv \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.equiv\") membawa perbezaan kedua-dua pengendali ke tertib normal terlebih dahulu kemudian menguji bahawa setiap pekali berada di bawah toleransi. Ia ialah perbandingan yang hampir selalu anda mahukan:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The method `simplify` alone leaves the two forms apart, because it merges only identical written terms. Likewise, [`is_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.is_hermitian \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.is_hermitian\") compares an operator with its adjoint in normal order, so it recognizes $b\\,b^\\dagger + b^\\dagger b$ as Hermitian without further work.\n"
msgstr "Kaedah `simplify` sahaja membiarkan kedua-dua bentuk berasingan, kerana ia hanya menggabungkan sebutan tertulis yang serupa. Begitu juga, [`is_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.is_hermitian \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.is_hermitian\") membandingkan pengendali dengan adjoinnya dalam tertib normal, jadi ia mengenali $b\\,b^\\dagger + b^\\dagger b$ sebagai Hermitian tanpa kerja tambahan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Normal ordering is an exact identity in the untruncated algebra, and `equiv` relies on that. It is *not* an identity after a truncation. A mapped operator depends on the form you map, so the mapped images of `contracted` and `reordered` above differ, on the highest retained level only. See [Truncate the Fock space](mappers#truncation-explanation) for the size of the difference and how to choose a form.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Tertib normal ialah identiti tepat dalam aljabar tidak terpangkas, dan `equiv` bergantung padanya. Ia *bukan* identiti selepas pemangkasan. Pengendali terpeta bergantung pada bentuk yang anda petakan, jadi imej terpeta bagi `contracted` dan `reordered` di atas berbeza, pada aras terpelihara tertinggi sahaja. Lihat [Memangkas ruang Fock](mappers#truncation-explanation) untuk saiz perbezaan dan cara memilih bentuk.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Order and filter terms {#order-and-filter-terms}"
msgstr "Menyusun dan menapis sebutan {#order-and-filter-terms}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Reordering the *terms* of an operator, as opposed to the factors inside a term, does not change the operator but can change the behavior of algorithms that read the terms in order, such as a randomized product formula. The functions of [`qiskit_bosons.operators.terms`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-terms#module-qiskit_bosons.operators.terms \"qiskit_bosons.operators.terms\") return a new operator and keep any group indices attached to their terms.\n"
msgstr "Menyusun semula *sebutan* pengendali, berbeza daripada faktor dalam sebutan, tidak mengubah pengendali tetapi boleh mengubah tingkah laku algoritma yang membaca sebutan mengikut tertib, seperti formula hasil darab rawak. Fungsi [`qiskit_bosons.operators.terms`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-terms#module-qiskit_bosons.operators.terms \"qiskit_bosons.operators.terms\") mengembalikan pengendali baharu dan mengekalkan sebarang indeks kumpulan yang dilampirkan pada sebutannya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[`canonical_order()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-terms-canonical-order#qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.canonical_order \"qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.canonical_order\") sorts the terms into a fixed order that depends only on the written factors, so an operator reads the same no matter how it was assembled. [`order_terms()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-terms-order-terms#qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.order_terms \"qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.order_terms\") sorts by a key that you supply, which receives each term as the tuple that [`iter_terms()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.iter_terms \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.iter_terms\") yields:\n"
msgstr "[`canonical_order()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-terms-canonical-order#qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.canonical_order \"qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.canonical_order\") mengisih sebutan ke dalam tertib tetap yang hanya bergantung pada faktor tertulis, jadi pengendali kelihatan sama walau bagaimana ia dipasang. [`order_terms()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-terms-order-terms#qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.order_terms \"qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.order_terms\") mengisih mengikut kunci yang anda berikan, yang menerima setiap sebutan sebagai tuple yang dihasilkan oleh [`iter_terms()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.iter_terms \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.iter_terms\"):\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If an operator carries group indices (see [Group operator terms: use the operator structure](grouping#grouping-explanation)), the function [`group_order()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-terms-group-order#qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.group_order \"qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.group_order\") makes each group one contiguous run of terms:\n"
msgstr "Jika pengendali membawa indeks kumpulan (lihat [Mengumpulkan sebutan pengendali: gunakan struktur pengendali](grouping#grouping-explanation)), fungsi [`group_order()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-terms-group-order#qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.group_order \"qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.group_order\") menjadikan setiap kumpulan satu rentetan sebutan bersebelahan:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The last helper removes terms rather than reordering them. A term that is a product of number operators, $b_i^\\dagger b_i$, only multiplies each Fock state by a phase, so [`filter_diagonal_terms()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-terms-filter-diagonal-terms#qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.filter_diagonal_terms \"qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.filter_diagonal_terms\") can drop the constant, the number operators, and their products when that phase is irrelevant for what you compute. It changes the operator *in place* and requires a normal-ordered operator, which it does not check:\n"
msgstr "Pembantu terakhir membuang sebutan dan bukannya menyusun semula. Sebutan yang merupakan hasil darab pengendali nombor, $b_i^\\dagger b_i$, hanya mendarab setiap keadaan Fock dengan fasa, jadi [`filter_diagonal_terms()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-terms-filter-diagonal-terms#qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.filter_diagonal_terms \"qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.filter_diagonal_terms\") boleh membuang pemalar, pengendali nombor, dan hasil darabnya apabila fasa itu tidak relevan bagi apa yang anda kira. Ia mengubah pengendali *di tempat* dan memerlukan pengendali bertertib normal, yang tidak disemaknya:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Only the two hopping terms remain. The on-site interaction and the number operator are diagonal in the occupation basis, so they are removed together with the constant. The repeated mode in the interaction is handled correctly: $b_0^\\dagger b_0^\\dagger b_0 b_0$ is diagonal, while $b_0^\\dagger b_0^\\dagger b_0$ would not be.\n"
msgstr "Hanya dua sebutan lompatan yang tinggal. Interaksi dalam-tapak dan pengendali nombor adalah pepenjuru dalam asas penghunian, jadi ia dibuang bersama pemalar. Mod berulang dalam interaksi dikendalikan dengan betul: $b_0^\\dagger b_0^\\dagger b_0 b_0$ ialah pepenjuru, manakala $b_0^\\dagger b_0^\\dagger b_0$ bukan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next steps {#next-steps}"
msgstr "Langkah seterusnya {#next-steps}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[Group operator terms: use the operator structure](grouping#grouping-explanation) shows how to tag terms with group indices.\n"
msgstr "[Mengumpulkan sebutan pengendali: gunakan struktur pengendali](grouping#grouping-explanation) menunjukkan cara menanda sebutan dengan indeks kumpulan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[Map operator representations](mappers#mappers-explanation) turns an operator into a qubit operator, including the choice of encoding and the effect of a truncation.\n"
msgstr "[Memetakan perwakilan pengendali](mappers#mappers-explanation) menukar pengendali kepada pengendali qubit, termasuk pilihan pengekodan dan kesan pemangkasan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[Work with bosonic circuits](circuit#bosonic-circuit-explanation) places an operator into a circuit as an [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate.\n"
msgstr "[Bekerja dengan litar bosonik](circuit#bosonic-circuit-explanation) meletakkan pengendali ke dalam litar sebagai gate [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution\").\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[Simulate Bose-Hubbard dynamics with a choice of encoding](bose-hubbard#bose-hubbard-getting-started) builds the Hamiltonian of a Bose-Hubbard chain and simulates it end to end.\n"
msgstr "[Mensimulasikan dinamik Bose-Hubbard dengan pilihan pengekodan](bose-hubbard#bose-hubbard-getting-started) membina Hamiltonian bagi rantai Bose-Hubbard dan mensimulasikannya dari hujung ke hujung.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The [`qiskit_bosons.operators`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators#module-qiskit_bosons.operators \"qiskit_bosons.operators\") and [`qiskit_bosons.operators.terms`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-terms#module-qiskit_bosons.operators.terms \"qiskit_bosons.operators.terms\") modules document the complete interface.\n"
msgstr "Modul [`qiskit_bosons.operators`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators#module-qiskit_bosons.operators \"qiskit_bosons.operators\") dan [`qiskit_bosons.operators.terms`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-terms#module-qiskit_bosons.operators.terms \"qiskit_bosons.operators.terms\") mendokumenkan antara muka lengkap.\n"
